<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shi Le</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">274–333</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shi Le was a Jie warlord who rose from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> to become a general of the Han-Zhao state, helping to capture the Jin capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> in 311. In 319 he broke away and founded the Later Zhao, and in 329 he destroyed Former Zhao, making Later Zhao the strongest state in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. He took the title of emperor in 330.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shi-le.jpg" alt="Shi Le" width="320" height="338" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Qian Xuan (formerly attributed), Freer Gallery of Art (owner) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shi_Le_(Emperor_Ming_of_Later_Zhao).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
